{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffSize","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","title":"MXLStaffSize","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some cases, a staff-size different than 100 also scales the notation on the staff, such as with a cue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff. In other cases, such as percussion staves, the lines may be more widely spaced without scaling the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation on the staff. The scaling attribute allows these two cases to be distinguished. It specifies the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percentage scaling that applies to the notation. Values less that 100 make the notation smaller while values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over 100 make the notation larger. The staff-size content and scaling attribute are both non-negative decimal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-size>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffsize"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/init(value:scaling:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/scaling","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/value"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-size element indicates how large a staff space is on this staff, expressed as a percentage of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work’s default scaling. Values less than 100 make the staff space smaller while values over 100 make the staff","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"space larger. A staff-type of cue, ossia, or editorial implies a staff-size of less than 100, but the exact","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is implementation-dependent unless specified here. Staff size affects staff height only, not the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relationship of the staff to the left and right margins.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffSize/scali